# Branch and PR workflow

`master` is the default branch. The only direct commit to it is the initial repository foundation.

- Start every feature or fix from current `master` on a new branch (`feature/<topic>` or `fix/<topic>`).
- Never commit feature or fix work to `master`; never push to `master` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Before switching branches, check for uncommitted changes. If the worktree is dirty, stop and ask the user.
- Deliver the branch as a pull request (`gh pr create`) with a summary and a test plan.
- Keep each PR below 100 changed files. Prefer cohesive, independently testable vertical slices; split a
  PR when review gets hard, but do not fragment tightly coupled code just to shrink it.
- Run `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` before pushing; CI must stay green.
